### Bug Scenario Description and Root Cause

The bug scenario involves a CascaderSelect component where, after searching and selecting all available options, the search results are not cleared automatically. This leaves the user on the search results page without a clear way to return to the full list, unless they click outside the dropdown to close and reopen it.

The root cause of the issue is that the search value is not being cleared when all items are selected in a multi-select scenario. The current implementation only clears the search value when the dropdown is closed or when a single item is selected.

### Bug Location and Analysis

The relevant code snippet is in the `handleChange` method of the `CascaderSelect` class. This method handles changes in selection and is responsible for updating the component's state, including the `searchValue`.

### Patch to Fix the Bug

To fix the issue, we need to ensure that the `searchValue` is cleared when all items are selected in a multi-select scenario. This can be done by adding a condition to clear the `searchValue` when the length of the selected values matches the length of the data source.

